<spell-notebook "list theming">
	<header level="1">
		List
		<header>A list is used to group related content.</>
	</>
	<list-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-list-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or on the
			list's box through `::part(list)`.

			- The items (and a nested list's items, through the `--ui-list-child-*` tokens) read them from the list, so set
			  them there or above, not on an item.
			- A variation (`spacing`, `celled` ...) swaps its own values in over yours.
			- Style an item's box with `ui-item::part(item)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-list {
			  --ui-list-item-border-color: var(--ui-primary);
			  --ui-list-item-padding-block: 0.5em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>Never set the `--_ui-list-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-list" playground>
				<ui-list>
					<ui-item>Apples</>
					<ui-item>Pears</>
					<ui-item>Oranges</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Each theme of the set (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes a list's colours and type through the
			shared tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
